{"name":"Paddle Wheel","hex":"#88724d","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"paddle wheel","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A large wheel, fitted with paddles, used to propel a vessel (especially a paddle steamer)"]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/paddle_wheel"}],"entries":[{"title":"Paddle wheel","blocks":[{"text":"A paddle wheel is a form of waterwheel or impeller in which a number of paddles are set around the periphery of the wheel. It has several uses, of which some are:"},{"items":["Very low-lift water pumping, such as flooding paddy fields at no more than about 0.5 m (20 in) height above the water source.","To move and mix algae culture in the raceway ponds used for algaculture.","Propulsion of watercraft","Low head hydro power","Flow sensors","Aerators"]}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/9f/Paddlewheel_aerator.jpg/330px-Paddlewheel_aerator.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Paddle_wheel","wikidata":"Q1874394"},{"title":"Paddle","blocks":[{"text":"A paddle is a handheld tool with an elongated handle and a flat, widened end used as a lever to apply force onto the bladed end. It most commonly describes a completely handheld tool used to propel a human-powered watercraft by pushing water in a direction opposite to the direction of travel. A paddle is different from an oar – an oar is attached to the watercraft via a fulcrum."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/5/52/Raft_paddle.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Paddle","wikidata":"Q599797"},{"title":"Wheel","blocks":[{"text":"A wheel is a rotating component intended to turn on an axle bearing. The wheel is one of the key components of the wheel and axle, which is one of the six simple machines. Wheels, in conjunction with axles, allow heavy objects to be moved easily, facilitating transportation, supporting loads, and performing work in machines. Wheels are also used for other purposes, such as a ship's wheel, steering wheel, potter's wheel, and flywheel."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/de/Landesmuseum_W%C3%BCrttemberg_Kelten_011.4.jpg/330px-Landesmuseum_W%C3%BCrttemberg_Kelten_011.4.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Wheel","wikidata":"Q446"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c5/Alecto_and_Rattler.jpg/330px-Alecto_and_Rattler.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c5/Alecto_and_Rattler.jpg/330px-Alecto_and_Rattler.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Contemporary lithograph of the competition between the propeller-driven Rattler (left) and paddle-driven Alecto (right) in 1845","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AAlecto_and_Rattler.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/52/Women_C-4_Canadian_cropped.jpg/500px-Women_C-4_Canadian_cropped.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/52/Women_C-4_Canadian_cropped.jpg/1280px-Women_C-4_Canadian_cropped.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/52/Women_C-4_Canadian_cropped.jpg/500px-Women_C-4_Canadian_cropped.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Team of the Boating Club de Canotage Otterburn using canoe paddles","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AWomen_C-4_Canadian_cropped.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/87/Paddel_Duvensee_Vitrine.jpg/500px-Paddel_Duvensee_Vitrine.jpg?u